For background, see #20400. We had previously rolled forward to go1.4.3 when we standardized the go version we ran on, but that caused regressions. Then we put everything on go1.5.3. That was better, and it took us longer to notice the regressions, but it's still not as good as go1.4.2, which #20577 reverted us to.

Obviously we can't stay on go1.4.2 forever, so we need to dig in and understand what the cause was. Note it may be (probably is?) a different cause for go1.4.3 and go1.5.3...

